# Line endings are pinned here instead of being left to each contributor's
# core.autocrlf. A CRLF checkout of a shipped hook is not cosmetic: bash reads
# `then\r` as a command, so the hook dies mid-verdict and every tool call it
# gates is denied with a syntax error (probe-verified: exit 2). The data files
# beside it fail more quietly: a trailing CR on a gentle-manifest.txt line makes
# every `[ -e "$CLAUDE_DIR/$rel" ]` test miss, so the legacy cleanup removes
# nothing, announces 0 and is confirmed removed by verify.sh — three layers
# agreeing over a cleanup that never ran — and claude-global.md is copied
# verbatim into the operator's always-loaded CLAUDE.md, whose budget check counts
# every byte it would gain.
#
# ONE rule for the whole tree, because naming the files one at a time has already
# been reopened twice: the shell layer was pinned, then those two data files, and
# plugin/hooks/hooks.json was still the single file inside verify.sh's CR scan
# with no entry here. windows-latest checks out under core.autocrlf=true, so that
# file arrived CRLF, failed the scan, and made the rendered-hooks comparison
# report every line of an unchanged manifest as diverged. codex/hooks/hooks.json,
# hook-hashes.txt, hook-gates.txt and every .md the installer copies verbatim
# were the same class waiting their turn; a glob per extension only moves the
# boundary to whichever extension lands next.
#
# `text=auto` rather than `text`, so a binary added later is decided by its own
# content instead of needing a line here. Every tracked file today is text and
# none carries a CR byte, so this normalizes nothing that already exists — it
# holds what arrives.
#
# The Windows entry points are the one place this contradicts the platform
# convention: install.bat, verify.bat and install.ps1 are LF in this tree today,
# so LF is the form that has actually been exercised, and CRLF would ship a form
# nothing here has run. Reversing that takes an override line under this one and
# a run behind it; verify.sh check 11 scans all three for CR bytes either way.
#
# No pin here is the whole fix: .gitattributes renormalizes no clone that already
# exists, so the manifest's three readers strip the CR themselves.
* text=auto eol=lf
